[thin] Deliberate functional C2 spring section: these ranked surface groups belong to the six free jaws above the tube equators, four on the fore Reservoir A pair and two on the V-A feed seat. Their measured 2.400 mm wall is the C2 section Derek selected with the 6.35 mm bore on Mark2 task 1379240291, recorded in future/snap-fit-tests/2026-10-26-mark2-combined/physical-result.json. Ordinary stock below the equators remains filled; the V-A seat has a full-width root from the plain lid to its Z268.970 tube axis. Only the working upper jaws use this specific flexure exception. This answer preserves the thinness ranking and establishes no full-lid force, lifetime or print result.
alternatives: Increasing the jaws to 3 mm while keeping the same bore increases each outer radius by 0.6 mm and changes the selected spring section. On the fore pair it also consumes 1.2 mm of spread space: preserving the current conservative 1 mm-per-jaw envelope and its 0.35 mm opposing gap requires wider tube spacing and another routing change. Filling above the equators joins the free jaws and closes the press-in mouths. A rigid cradle with a separate closure adds a part and an assembly step instead of providing the selected direct snap.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
