[sliver] The strip reading measures the 0.75 mm projection of each functional J1/J2 retaining lip, not the hook's material thickness. Each lip has 3 mm stock behind its flat underside and spans the bank's full 16 mm cable width. The 2.2 mm seat depth, 0.75 mm lip and 45-degree entry use the accepted cable-hook section. The two lips retain the front-going leads in the separate J1 and J2 cavities; the seven-lead J1 grouping retains its stated physical-fit scope.
alternatives: Removing the projection opens the retaining mouth to the full seat depth and removes the selected capture. Filling below it occupies the cable cavity. Thickening the projection into that cavity changes the accepted entry and retention section. This finding conflates the functional lip's reach with a thin structural wall.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
click: x=131.200 y=74.825 z=23.700
click: x=131.200 y=80.025 z=18.150

[ledge] Functional flat retaining undersides of the J1/J2 cable hooks. Each 12 mm2 face is the 0.75 mm projection across the 16 mm cable span, backed by 3 mm hook stock. Its flat underside catches the leads beneath the 45-degree entry. The 2.2 mm seat depth, lip and entry follow the accepted cable-hook section; the installed seven-lead J1 grouping has its own physical-fit scope. Tree(auto)/Default supplies the current native support decisions.
alternatives: Removing or sloping the retaining underside changes the selected cable capture; filling beneath it closes the cable seat. The overhang is the named retaining interface, rather than a cut remnant between unrelated features.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
click: x=128.533 y=74.700 z=23.700
click: x=128.533 y=79.900 z=18.150

[thin] Specific straight B-fill passage roof: the Ø6.8 round passage and its 0.25 mm supported-roof allowance leave 2.20 mm of stock beneath the Z253.4 equipment face, at native Z5.20–7.40. This is the straight tube entrance leading to the separate R14 holder clearance window; the holder remains with the tube and cured foam. Its current native slice has one support body accessible through the open B-fill window before loading the tube.
alternatives: A 3 mm roof above the same passage grows 0.8 mm above the equipment face, into the PCB/service envelope. Lowering the roof reduces the selected tube passage; moving the passage changes its fixed fore entrance and reservoir route. Opening its full straight top removes the tube-bearing roof and the solid dry-seam surface under the foil.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
click: x=112.234 y=-43.524 z=7.400
click: x=112.234 y=-43.524 z=5.200

[sliver] Functional retaining underside of the approved Reservoir A level-lead hook. Its 0.75 mm projection closes the 2.20 mm seat to a 1.45 mm entry mouth for nominal 1.70 mm insulation, matching the accepted cable clip's entry section. The flat underside catches the five leads after insertion. The hook's walls and full floor retain 3 mm structural stock.
alternatives: A 3 mm projection closes this seat completely; retaining the same mouth with that projection requires a 4.45 mm deep seat, adding 2.25 mm of cable movement behind the catch. Reducing the projection opens the mouth toward the conductor diameter. Sloping the underside supplies an exit ramp instead of a flat catch.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
click: x=-100.200 y=-73.175 z=20.000

[ledge] Functional flat catch of the approved Reservoir A level-lead hook. The accepted 0.75 mm retaining projection and 1.45 mm mouth retain nominal 1.70 mm insulated leads; the entry chamfer is on the opposite side of this face.
alternatives: A sloped underside lets the cable cam out through the mouth. Increasing the projection to 3 mm requires a 4.45 mm deep seat to preserve the mouth, adding 2.25 mm of movement behind the catch. Filling the entry prevents insertion from above.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
click: x=-102.867 y=-73.300 z=20.000

[thin] Specific 4 mm flavor-line flexures: these four free jaws use the C2 profile scaled from the 6.35 mm section to the 4 mm bore, giving a 1.52 mm working jaw. Their mouths permit direct press-in insertion; the filled roots retain 3 mm stock. The smaller section is a defined spring, with no transferred claim about measured force or fatigue.
alternatives: A 3 mm jaw changes the spring section and mouth compliance. Filling above the tube equator closes the loading mouth; a rigid saddle with a separate closure adds a part and an assembly step.
file: hardware/printed-parts/cold-core/foam-cap/foam-cap-lid-top.step
